A||||3||Bautsch||Front End Shake
Z||000000||Bautsch||08-12-99||11:33 AM||||The Fiero I just purchased has a little bit of shake in the steering wheel during braking. Would anybody know if this is most likely just a brake problem or would it be a steering or suspension problem?<p>Thanks,<p>Mike Bautsch<br>mike@macvend.com
Z||000001||86_Fastback||08-12-99||11:45 AM||||It sounds like your rotors are warped.  It is one of the signs of warping.  New rotors and pads should be too if you do the work yourself.<br>-Gregg
Z||000002||stsmithgt||08-20-99||10:09 PM||||It could be as simple as a tire out of balance. Are the rims true?  Or a worn out shock.  Check for leaks.  A shock can allow a tire to bounce down the road which would definately put a shake in the steering wheel.  
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||08-28-99||11:31 PM||||i was getting that too.. it turned out all i had to do was remove the horn button, and re-tighten all the screws
